{title: Father of Tents}
{subtitle: Genesis 4:20; 4:19–24}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | [Ab] [Bb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Lamech took two wives for himself [Bb/D]
[Cm7]One was named Adah, [Ab]the other Zil[Bb]lah
[Eb]Adah gave birth to a son [Bb/D]
[Cm7]His name was Jabal in the land [Ab][Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]He was the father of those [Bb]who live in tents
[Eb]And keep live[Bb/D]stock under the o[Cm7]pen sky
[Ab]Walking the paths that he had [Bb]made
A no[Eb]madic life [Bb/D]beginning to [Cm7]rise [Ab][Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]In the line of Cain he [Bb/D]stood
[Cm7]Part of a family growing [Ab]wide [Bb]
[Eb]Jubal played the lyre and [Bb/D]pipe
[Cm7]Tu-bal-Cain forged the bronze and i[Ab]ron [Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]He was the father of those [Bb]who live in tents
[Eb]And keep live[Bb/D]stock under the o[Cm7]pen sky
[Ab]Walking the paths that he had [Bb]made
A no[Eb]madic [Bb/D]life beginning to [Cm7]rise [Ab]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]Before the flood the world was [Bb]young
[Eb]Cultural pioneers finding their [Ab]way
[Cm7]Tents and flocks in the ancient [Bb]days
[Ab]Living out the promise of the land
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Father of those who live in [Bb]tents
[Eb]Keeping the live[Bb/D]stock through the [Cm7]years
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
